{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq7l4im5b3q","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"wincase-c (variant C) NULL — rigging guard failed; single-task memory-win premise falsified (0 wins in 8)","summary":"Phase 1 falsification of the cross-session winning-case experiment, variant C (real task→transcript resolveOwner). Built an honest anti-v4 trap: strategy-silent spec (bench/specs/wincase-c.md), programmatic 25-row acceptance fixture (bench/sandbox/wincase-resolve.test.js) where ~40% of rows have empty agent records recoverable ONLY by time-window overlap correlation against byWindow; naive direct+session impl fails 11 rows, correct correlation impl passes 29/0. Seeded note A (note-mq7kyiir6sx) verified as #1 semantic hit in workspace /Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude. RIGGING GUARD FAILED: cold-B (arm off, no MCP) solved 3/3, each independently deriving the full window-correlation resolver by READING the committed test (mean H≈5805, W≈458, 3 explorers, ~40s). Trap is SELF-SOLVABLE → INVALID. Did NOT run the warm arm; NO win claimed. The single-task memory-win premise is FALSIFIED even under the most favorable authentic trap. Still 0 wins in 8 attempts (v1–v7 + wincase-c). ROOT CAUSE is structural: a committed, fully-specified acceptance test for a pure function leaves no empirical gap — the test IS the strategy reveal, so prose-silence can't create one. Fix paths: held-out (unreadable) test, a live-runtime-quirk task, or abandon single-task pure-function and pivot to multi-task/cross-session winning cases.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-10T04:44:56.765Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
